   - `pulseInterval`: The interval at which the dot should pulse (every second).
   - `lastPulseTime`: Tracks the last time the dot pulsed.
   - `requestAnimationFrame`: Ensures smooth animation by syncing with the browser's repaint cycle.
   - `setTimeout`: Handles the pulse effect by changing the scale and reverting it back after a short duration.

### Code Implementation

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Pulse Animation</title>
<style>
  .pulse-animation {
    width: 100%;
    height: 32px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .pulse-line {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    background-color: red;
  }

  .pulse-dot {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    background-color: blue;
    border-radius: 50%;
    transition: transform 0.5s ease-in-out;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="pulse-animation">
  <div class="pulse-line"></div>
  <div class="pulse-dot"></div>
</div>

<script>
  const pulseDot = document.querySelector('.pulse-dot');
  const pulseLine = document.querySelector('.pulse-line');
  const container = document.querySelector('.pulse-animation');
  const containerWidth = container.offsetWidth;
  const dotWidth = pulseDot.offsetWidth;

  let isPulsing = false;
  let currentPos = 0;
  const pulseInterval = 1000; // Pulse every second
  let lastPulseTime = 0;

  function moveDot() {
    if (currentPos + dotWidth >= containerWidth) {
      currentPos = 0;
    } else {
      currentPos += 2; // Adjust the speed here
    }

    pulseDot.style.left = `${currentPos}px`;

    const currentTime = Date.now();
    if (currentTime - lastPulseTime >= pulseInterval && !isPulsing) {
      isPulsing = true;
      pulseDot.style.transform = 'translateY(-50%) scaleY(4)'; // Increase height to 32px (8px * 4)
      setTimeout(() => {
        pulseDot.style.transform = 'translateY(-50%) scaleY(1)'; // Return to original size
        isPulsing = false;
        lastPulseTime = currentTime;
      }, 500); // Duration of the pulse
    }

    requestAnimationFrame(moveDot);
  }

  moveDot();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of the Triangular Waveform Effect

The triangular waveform effect is achieved by scaling the dot's height. When the dot pulses, its height is increased to 32px (which is the height of the container). This is done by setting the `scaleY` property to 4 (since the original height of the dot is 8px, 4 * 8px = 32px). The dot then returns to its original size after a short duration, creating the triangular waveform effect.

